(158038, 8566, 4648, '<td valign="top">Looks so neat.  Good focus   Good crop   Good colors.  Great depth  Meets challenge well.  PTL  Good shot</td>', 'Looks so neat.  Good focus   Good crop   Good colors.  Great depth  Meets challenge well.  PTL  Good shot', '2002-11-23 22:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158039, 8566, 2553, '<td valign="top">This shot is so cool.  I can''t wait to see the photo info on it.  I would love to try something like this.  A very dynamic composition with interesting lighting.  One of my highest rated.  lhall</td>', 'This shot is so cool.  I can''t wait to see the photo info on it.  I would love to try something like this.  A very dynamic composition with interesting lighting.  One of my highest rated.  lhall', '2002-11-24 12:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158040, 8566, 2221, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone who commented. Nice to see that other people enjoy the photo, too. It wasn''t an UFO ;-) The streaks of light come from a bus driving along the street. I chose the title (and think it fits to the challenge topic) because bridges are an important technology and always have been vital links between cities and people in general.<br/><br/>The photo was only cropped and scaled. I did not do any heavy postprocessing to it. The colouring comes from the white balance I chose. I set it to "night" if I remember correctly and not to the one matching the lamps on the street. That''s why the photo has this golden tint, which I like on this photo. I also did not sharpen it. The jagged edges come from the JPEG compression. I maxed out the quality to fit the 150 kB limit but it still was not enough.<br/><br/>I still wonder why not more people complained about the lens flare created by the lamp to the upper right (not seen on the photo). This really annoyed me and I tried to get rid of it by going some steps backward and zooming more in, but it didn''t help much. Also unfortunately there came no bus again.<br/><br/></td>', 'Thanks to everyone who commented. Nice to see that other people enjoy the photo, too. It wasn''t an UFO ;-) The streaks of light come from a bus driving along the street. I chose the title (and think it fits to the challenge topic) because bridges are an important technology and always have been vital links between cities and people in general.The photo was only cropped and scaled. I did not do any heavy postprocessing to it. The colouring comes from the white balance I chose. I set it to "night" if I remember correctly and not to the one matching the lamps on the street. That''s why the photo has this golden tint, which I like on this photo. I also did not sharpen it. The jagged edges come from the JPEG compression. I maxed out the quality to fit the 150 kB limit but it still was not enough.I still wonder why not more people complained about the lens flare created by the lamp to the upper right (not seen on the photo). This really annoyed me and I tried to get rid of it by going some steps backward and zooming more in, but it didn''t help much. Also unfortunately there came no bus again.', '2002-11-25 09:27:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(158041, 8568, 674, '<td valign="top">Technically correct , exposure, focus, saturation , contrast. 8<br/>Good composition.  6<br/>Tells a story or creates a mood 6<br/>      Impact to the viewer <br/>Relevance to the Challenge 9<br/>Overall 8<br/>sulamk<br/></td>', 'Technically correct , exposure, focus, saturation , contrast. 8Good composition.  6Tells a story or creates a mood 6      Impact to the viewer Relevance to the Challenge 9Overall 8sulamk', '2002-11-18 01:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158042, 8568, 2170, '<td valign="top">I don''t think the rustic (or just rusty) nature of this equipment really says "technology" to me.</td>', 'I don''t think the rustic (or just rusty) nature of this equipment really says "technology" to me.', '2002-11-18 12:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158043, 8568, 3575, '<td valign="top">A little out of focus but very interesting. I don''t see how it could still be a functioning mechanism with the amount of rust and decay...I like that I stayed and studied this for a while. Good job. joann</td>', 'A little out of focus but very interesting. I don''t see how it could still be a functioning mechanism with the amount of rust and decay...I like that I stayed and studied this for a while. Good job. joann', '2002-11-18 16:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158044, 8568, 327, '<td valign="top">Love rust. Might of been a bit too bright there in the sunshine, although I like the shot.</td>', 'Love rust. Might of been a bit too bright there in the sunshine, although I like the shot.', '2002-11-18 19:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158045, 8568, 4177, '<td valign="top">My feeling is that the shadows are too harsh for this picture and don''t contribute. I think pushing more light into the dark places (with white reflectors) would have enhanced the overall impact of the picture.</td>', 'My feeling is that the shadows are too harsh for this picture and don''t contribute. I think pushing more light into the dark places (with white reflectors) would have enhanced the overall impact of the picture.', '2002-11-18 20:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158046, 8568, 3532, '<td valign="top">I would like to see more detail in the shadow areas.</td>', 'I would like to see more detail in the shadow areas.', '2002-11-20 20:38:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158047, 8568, 4514, '<td valign="top">hmmmm.  Well could be better.</td>', 'hmmmm.  Well could be better.', '2002-11-20 21:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158048, 8568, 1280, '<td valign="top">I like all the rust in this picture.  Composition is a little cluttered.  I think you included too much in here.  Maybe a tighter crop to eliminate things like the building on the left, and the cut off light up on the right. I sincerely hope these suggestions help, and please remember they are only MY ideas.  Grayce</td>', 'I like all the rust in this picture.  Composition is a little cluttered.  I think you included too much in here.  Maybe a tighter crop to eliminate things like the building on the left, and the cut off light up on the right. I sincerely hope these suggestions help, and please remember they are only MY ideas.  Grayce', '2002-11-22 23:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158049, 8568, 4648, '<td valign="top">Great shot.  Show this to the high up there and tell them they need to paint before the bridge rusts away and falls.  It''s the rust that adds authenticity to the shot and makes it interesting, not squeeky clean bridge.  Good focus.  In fact, nice techs all the way around.  Just needs a little more "wow" to jump out and grab you.  PTL</td>', 'Great shot.  Show this to the high up there and tell them they need to paint before the bridge rusts away and falls.  It''s the rust that adds authenticity to the shot and makes it interesting, not squeeky clean bridge.  Good focus.  In fact, nice techs all the way around.  Just needs a little more "wow" to jump out and grab you.  PTL', '2002-11-23 22:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158050, 8571, 4267, '<td valign="top">needs less light</td>', 'needs less light', '2002-11-18 01:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158051, 8571, 3273, '<td valign="top">The CD seems over saturated and slightly out of focus.  Nice original idea though.</td>', 'The CD seems over saturated and slightly out of focus.  Nice original idea though.', '2002-11-18 04:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158052, 8571, 3540, '<td valign="top">The whole image is a little grainy.  Looks like a little despeckle wouldn''t hurt either.  It''s a pretty good idea, but there is some areas that just aren''t as crisp as they should be.  Good luck - Inspzil</td>', 'The whole image is a little grainy.  Looks like a little despeckle wouldn''t hurt either.  It''s a pretty good idea, but there is some areas that just aren''t as crisp as they should be.  Good luck - Inspzil', '2002-11-18 05:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158053, 8571, 2344, '<td valign="top">Looks soft. Could be the focus or the compression</td>', 'Looks soft. Could be the focus or the compression', '2002-11-18 07:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(158054, 8571, 811, '<td valign="top">A bit more contrast so that the grays didn''t all run together would have made this shot totally awesome.  It is still great, I just have that one little nit-pick about it. 10 karmat</td>', 'A bit more contrast so that the grays didn''t all run together would have made this shot totally awesome.  It is still great, I just have that one little nit-pick about it. 10 karmat', '2002-11-18 14:38:00.000000', NULL, 1),
