(159025, 8647, 3859, '<td valign="top">This is so very clever!  I love the yellow color, but the color of the memory stick makes it look like a Hershey''s chocolate bar.  Because I use memory sticks, I know that they don''t normally look like that! And that''s really the only thing I would change. 8</td>', 'This is so very clever!  I love the yellow color, but the color of the memory stick makes it look like a Hershey''s chocolate bar.  Because I use memory sticks, I know that they don''t normally look like that! And that''s really the only thing I would change. 8', '2002-11-20 12:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159026, 8647, 811, '<td valign="top">That would be one way to smuggle sticks if you had to for some reason.  The focus and lighting is awesome, but the yellow cast is distracting.  I am assuming the memory stick is purple, but it looks kinda bluish-bronze with the yellow in it.   Otherwise, awesome shot! karmat</td>', 'That would be one way to smuggle sticks if you had to for some reason.  The focus and lighting is awesome, but the yellow cast is distracting.  I am assuming the memory stick is purple, but it looks kinda bluish-bronze with the yellow in it.   Otherwise, awesome shot! karmat', '2002-11-20 15:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(159027, 8647, 772, '<td valign="top">I really like the concept on this photo... The yellow on yellow works very well, and I also like the strong diagonal in this image.  The only problem *I* see in this image is the white balance.  Most wouldn''t notice this, but that memory stick has taken on a yellow tint from its normal light blue color.  Regardless of that, I still think this is an excellent shot... good work :) - setzler</td>', 'I really like the concept on this photo... The yellow on yellow works very well, and I also like the strong diagonal in this image.  The only problem *I* see in this image is the white balance.  Most wouldn''t notice this, but that memory stick has taken on a yellow tint from its normal light blue color.  Regardless of that, I still think this is an excellent shot... good work :) - setzler', '2002-11-20 17:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
