(293467, 8556, 6999, '<td valign="top">As far as the challenge goes (or went, rather) this is a great subject: has all the shininess, brightness and lots of buttons that is what the challenge calls for. There are a few things I''d have done differently, even when shooting at this angle - DOF is perhaps too shallow - the LED display that grabs the eye for it''s brightness (and also because that''s where one looks for information) is just outside the range of focus. There''s quite a bit of noise here too - especially in the blue, which certainly doesn''t help the high-tech quality. And I think I''d have shot from further away and used the zoom, if one were available, to avoid the distortion you''ve got from the lens. Actually, I think i''d have shot at a more diagonal angle, and reflected some light from the thing - the gleams would have helped emphasise the modernness.