(157700, 8541, 4648, '<td valign="top">What is the dark 1/4 of the picture besides a waste.  The next 1/4 meets the challenge.  And the last 1/2 is all empty space again.  Focus is clear but that is about all.  1/4 of 10 points is 2.5 so I can''t give you more than that for composition and another 1/5 for focus gives you a 4.  Wanted you to know how I arrived at such low score so you could see it is a fair score.  Sorry  PTL</td>', 'What is the dark 1/4 of the picture besides a waste.  The next 1/4 meets the challenge.  And the last 1/2 is all empty space again.  Focus is clear but that is about all.  1/4 of 10 points is 2.5 so I can''t give you more than that for composition and another 1/5 for focus gives you a 4.  Wanted you to know how I arrived at such low score so you could see it is a fair score.  Sorry  PTL', '2002-11-23 12:35:00.000000', NULL, 1);
<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Ed<br/> <br/>Think I''d have given you a 4, with that many technical gripes.</td>', 'As far as the challenge goes (or went, rather) this is a great subject: has all the shininess, brightness and lots of buttons that is what the challenge calls for. There are a few things I''d have done differently, even when shooting at this angle - DOF is perhaps too shallow - the LED display that grabs the eye for it''s brightness (and also because that''s where one looks for information) is just outside the range of focus. There''s quite a bit of noise here too - especially in the blue, which certainly doesn''t help the high-tech quality. And I think I''d have shot from further away and used the zoom, if one were available, to avoid the distortion you''ve got from the lens. Actually, I think i''d have shot at a more diagonal angle, and reflected some light from the thing - the gleams would have helped emphasise the modernness. Cheers Ed Think I''d have given you a 4, with that many technical gripes.', '2003-05-09 16:01:43.000000', NULL, 0),
